2650 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186072654 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072650 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186072655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072650 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072650 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072650 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "abb08e94-171f-5a46-890c-cb2c4848e118" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072651 #edb/ref 1080 "There are exactly $2$ male members and exactly $3$ female members" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072651 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072651 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cd340739-993e-5646-a6ea-9ee601ff5acf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072652 #edb/ref 1080 "There are $2$ male members for every $5$ female members" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072652 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072652 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d844845d-7db2-527f-a1d5-581d6686c16b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072653 #edb/ref 1080 "There are $3$ male members for every $2$ female members" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072653 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072653 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e4612e89-991b-5682-ae83-c9c45029bd4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072654 #edb/ref 1080 "There are exactly $3$ male members and exactly $2$ female members" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072654 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072654 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56d367f8-2c2c-58a4-b513-183d9fe3438b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072655 #edb/ref 1080 "There are $2$ male members for every $3$ female members" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072655 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072655 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5f36f2c7-0744-5fb3-8453-baef888d7f3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073450 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13256" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073450 #edb/ref 1071 "What ratio describes the number of pentagons to the total number of shapes?\n\n![](images/0f/0fff5dd90ce40b76128001c25b41cf8f34a2b4f63c44717823ba0bdcc98ef224.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073450 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c4235bf2-0c2b-5c2d-be8d-779a8e5fb38f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073450 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of pentagons to the total number of shapes as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{number of pentagons}: \\textrm{total number of shapes}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of pentagons. There are $3$ pentagons.\n- Next, we count the total number of shapes. There are $6$ shapes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of pentagons to total shapes is $3:6$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073451 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13257" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073451 #edb/ref 1071 "A merchant has $8$ black crates and $5$ green crates. What ratio describes the number of green crates to the total number of crates?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073451 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76442c46-6958-556f-a895-027a3ce7427b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073451 #edb/ref 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of green crates to the total number of crates as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{number of green crates}: \\textrm{total number of crates}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the number of green crates. There are $5$ green crates.\n- Next, we count the total number of crates. There are $8+5 = 13$ crates.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of green crates to total crates is $5:13$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073452 #edb/ref 1069 "e-13258" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073452 #edb/ref 1071 "The ratio of red marbles to blue marbles in a bag is $7:8$. What is the meaning of this ratio?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073452 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "34ec50f1-1873-510d-8693-49f93bae1df8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073452 #edb/ref 1074 "If the ratio of red marbles to blue marbles is ${\\color{red}{7}}:{\\color{blue}{8}}$, it means that there are ${\\color{red}{7}}$ red marbles for every ${\\color{blue}{8}}$ blue marbles." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073735 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073735 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073735 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Ratio" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073735 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073735 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0be25cd8-4333-5e00-91e9-7e1256281814" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073736 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073736 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073736 #edb/ref 1039 "Word Problems" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073736 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073736 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "acde6034-9007-5777-a79c-5f99ead9154a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073737 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186073995 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073737 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186074402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073737 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073737 #edb/ref 1039 "Interpreting Ratios" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073737 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186073452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073737 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9edb7c90-39fa-5396-b00e-04a0627d0581" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073954 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073954 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073954 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073954 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073954 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073954 #edb/ref 1045 "Introduction to Ratios" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073954 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186074630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073954 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050924 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073954 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8d68098e-61ea-5694-8c81-2a07b3b89448" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074402 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186072650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074402 #edb/ref 1069 "q-60087" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074402 #edb/ref 1071 "The ratio of male to the female members of a chess club is $2: 3$. What is the meaning of this ratio?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074402 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6cd5b8a6-9fde-5a1d-8425-5a7cfba25b44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074630 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074631 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074630 #edb/ref 1061 185365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074630 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0340ef01-84ac-534c-a79b-d7336d5305b6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074630 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186075037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074631 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074632 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074631 #edb/ref 1061 185366 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074631 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "310791d0-15c7-54f2-9d96-846dc8064a94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074631 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074632 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074632 #edb/ref 1061 185369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074632 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb26c220-5990-5446-ae5f-4ca0b272e25a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074632 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073736 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074633 #edb/ref 1061 185372 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074633 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9ef29b30-f1cb-5cec-a28d-cd61e7444890" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074633 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075037 #edb/ref 1064 "A **ratio** is a mathematical statement that expresses the relative sizes of two quantities.\n\nAs an example, let's look at the triangles and circles below.\n\n![](images/48/4865786ce55e0ec3fc1747ece4ea962425a3f83b2a45c7980f52719522318c82.png)\n\nWe can express the ratio of the number of circles to the number of triangles as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{\\textrm{number of circles}}}: {\\color{red}{\\textrm{number of triangles}}}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of circles. There are $\\color{blue}5$ circles.\n- Next, we count the number of triangles. There are $\\color{red}2$ triangles.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of circles to triangles is ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}2}$.\n\nWe can describe this ratio in words as follows:\n\n> *The ratio of circles to triangles is ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}2}$ because there are ${\\color{blue}5}$ circles*for every*${\\color{red}{2}}$ triangles.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075037 #edb/ref 1065 8277 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075037 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3d8ebe22-8ef7-538a-a42d-4f1133689833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186075037 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
